-- url     : https://prove2.me/theorems/17ab59a0-80a7-5358-8305-b1f950ff2330
-- title:
--   Supersingular affine chart over the level field, case q=3
-- statement:
--   Throughout, $q$ is a prime subject to $q = 3$ (hypothesis `hq3`), $M'$ is a non-zero natural number with $q \nmid M'$, and $\ell_g$ is a prime with $\ell_g \equiv 11 \pmod{12}$ and $\ell_g \mid M'$.
--
--   **Valuation-theoretic and modular data.** $A$ is a valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ satisfying `A.LiesOverPrime q`, i.e. $q$ lies in the nonunits of $A$; write $\kappa = \mathrm{ResidueField}\,A$. Here `modularFunctionFieldC κ M'` is the intermediate field of $\kappa \subseteq \kappa((t))$ generated by the $q$-expansion $j_q$ of $j$ and by its $M'$-fold $q$-expansion rescaling, and a `Place` of it over $\kappa$ is a valuation subring containing $\kappa$, distinct from the whole field, whose ideals are principal, with $\operatorname{ord}$ the associated $\mathbb Z$-valued valuation and $\operatorname{evalAt}$ the residue value transported back to $\kappa$ along the structure map (and $0$ off the valuation subring). $W$ is a finite set of such places, and the hypothesis `hW` says that $W$ is exactly `ssPlaces q M' κ`, the set of places $w$ that are rational (the map $\kappa \to$ residue field of $w$ is surjective), satisfy the predicate `IsAffineGeomPlace`, and have $w.\mathrm{evalAt}(j_{\mathrm{geom}})$ in `ssJSet q κ`; $s$ is a chosen element of $W$.
--
--   The hypothesis `hle` asserts the inclusion $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldBar}\,M' \le \mathrm{fieldBar}\,q\,M'$ of intermediate fields of $\overline{\mathbb Q} \subseteq \overline{\mathbb Q}((t))$: on the left, the $\overline{\mathbb Q}$-field generated by the coefficientwise images of the full level-$M'$ modular function field $\mathbb Q(\,\mathrm{qExpand}_d\,j_q : d \mid M'\,)$; on the right, the base change to $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ of the function field of $X_H$ of level $q^2M'$ with $H = \mathrm{levelH}\,q\,M'$ the kernel of the reduction $(\mathbb Z/q^2M')^\times \to (\mathbb Z/q)^\times$, i.e. the units congruent to $1$ modulo $q$.
--
--   $R_0$ is a `ConstantReduction` of $A$ from $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldBar}\,M'$ to $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldC}\,\kappa\,M'$: a valuation subring $R_0.\mathrm{integers}$ of the former, a surjective ring homomorphism $R_0.\mathrm{residue}$ from it onto the latter with kernel the maximal ideal, a map $R_0.\mathrm{placeMap}$ on places, together with the axioms that $\mathrm{algebraMap}(x)$ lies in $R_0.\mathrm{integers}$ iff $x \in A$, that $R_0.\mathrm{residue}$ is compatible with the residue map of $A$ on constants, that every non-zero element of the big field becomes, after multiplication by a suitable constant, an element of $R_0.\mathrm{integers}$ with non-zero residue, that $R_0.\mathrm{placeMap}$ preserves degrees, and that $R_0.\mathrm{placeMap}$ pushes the divisor of an element with non-zero residue forward to the divisor of its residue. The hypothesis `hR₀` states that for every Laurent series $y$ over $A$ whose coefficientwise image in $\overline{\mathbb Q}((t))$ lies in $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldBar}\,M'$, that element belongs to $R_0.\mathrm{integers}$ and its $R_0$-residue, read as a Laurent series over $\kappa$, is the coefficientwise reduction of $y$.
--
--   **Small-field data.** $k_0$ is an intermediate field of $\mathbb Q \subseteq \overline{\mathbb Q}$ and $\pi_0 \in k_0$ has image in $A$ (`hπ`). Writing $A \cap k_0$ for the comap of $A$ along $k_0 \to \overline{\mathbb Q}$, the hypotheses require: $A \cap k_0$ is a discrete valuation ring (`hdvr`) whose maximal ideal is generated by $\pi_0$ (`hunif`), it is a henselian local ring (`hhens`), its residue field is algebraically closed (`hres`), and every $a \in A$ is congruent modulo the maximal ideal of $A$ to some element of $k_0 \cap A$ (`hκ`).
--
--   **Auxiliary roots of unity and uniformiser.** $\ell$ is a prime with $\ell \ge 3$, $\ell \ne q$ and $\ell \nmid M'$; $\zeta_0 \in k_0$ is a primitive $q\ell$-th root of unity in $\overline{\mathbb Q}$; and $\varpi_t \in k_0$ has image in $A$ (`hϖtA`) with $\varpi_t^{\,q^2-1} = q\,u$ for some unit $u$ of $A$ (`hϖt`).
--
--   **Base layer.** $K_b$ is an intermediate field of $k_0 \subseteq \overline{\mathbb Q}$ with $K_b = \bot$, so $K_b = k_0$; $A_b$ is a valuation subring of $K_b$ with $x \in A_b$ iff $x \in A$ (`hAb`), and $\varpi_b$ is a non-zero element of $A_b$ generating its maximal ideal.
--
--   **Conclusion.** Equip $\mathrm{fieldBar}\,q\,M'$ with the $k_0$-algebra structure obtained by composing $k_0 \to \overline{\mathbb Q}$ with $\overline{\mathbb Q} \to \mathrm{fieldBar}\,q\,M'$. Then for every intermediate field $F_0$ of $\mathrm{fieldBar}\,q\,M'$ over $k_0$ which is characterised by the condition that $f \in F_0$ if and only if every Laurent coefficient $f_n$ ($n \in \mathbb Z$) of $f$ lies in (the image of) $k_0$, there exists a valuation subring $W_0$ of $F_0$ with the following properties.
--
--   (1) For $x \in k_0$: the image of $x$ in $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ lies in $A$ if and only if the image of $x$ in $F_0$ lies in $W_0$.
--
--   (2) $W_0$ is a discrete valuation ring.
--
--   (3) The image of $\pi_0$ in $F_0$ lies in $W_0$ and generates the maximal ideal of $W_0$.
--
--   (4) Specialisation at $s$: for every Laurent series $g$ over $\mathbb Q$ lying in $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldFull}\,M'$ whose coefficientwise image in $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldBar}\,M'$ lies in $R_0.\mathrm{integers}$, and such that (i) for every place $P$ of $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldBar}\,M'$ over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$, $P.\mathrm{ord}$ of the image of $g$ is $\ge 0$ whenever $P.\mathrm{ord}$ of the image of $j_q$ is $\ge 0$, and (ii) the $R_0$-residue of $g$ lies in the valuation subring of the place $s$: the image of $g$ under the inclusion given by `hle` lies in $F_0$, the resulting element of $F_0$ lies in $W_0$, and for every $c \in k_0$ whose image lies in $A$ such that the residue of $c$ in $\kappa$ equals $s.\mathrm{evalAt}$ of the $R_0$-residue of $g$, the difference of that element of $F_0$ and the image of $c$ lies in $W_0$ and in the maximal ideal of $W_0$.
--
--   (5) Level stability: for every $\zeta \in \mathrm{Idx}\,q$ (a primitive $q$-th root of unity in $\overline{\mathbb Q}$), every $\gamma \in SL_2(\mathbb Z)$ with $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$, and every $f \in \mathrm{fieldBar}\,q\,M'$ with both $f \in F_0$ and $\mathrm{levelAutBar}\,q\,M'\,\zeta\,\gamma\,(f) \in F_0$: $f$ lies in $W_0$ if and only if $\mathrm{levelAutBar}\,q\,M'\,\zeta\,\gamma\,(f)$ does.
--
--   (6) An affine chart: there exist a subring $B$ of $\mathrm{fieldBar}\,q\,M'$ and an $A_b$-algebra structure on $B$ such that, writing $E$ for the intermediate field $k_0(\text{image of } K_b) \sqcup F_0$ inside $\mathrm{fieldBar}\,q\,M'$:
--
--   (a) the structure map sends $a \in A_b$ to the image of $a \in K_b \subseteq \overline{\mathbb Q}$ in $\mathrm{fieldBar}\,q\,M'$;
--
--   (b) $B \subseteq E$, and every element of $E$ is of the form $g/h$ with $g, h \in B$ and $h \ne 0$;
--
--   (c) $B$ is formally smooth and of finite presentation over $A_b$;
--
--   (d) $B/\varpi_b B$ has Krull dimension at most $1$;
--
--   (e) every element of $B$ lies in $F_0$ and, as such, in $W_0$;
--
--   (f) the image of $\varpi_b$ in $B$ is a prime element;
--
--   (g) an element $f$ of $F_0$ lies in $W_0$ if and only if $f = g/h$ for some $g, h \in B$ with $\varpi_b \nmid h$ in $B$;
--
--   (h) the image of $j_q$ in $\mathrm{fieldBar}\,q\,M'$ lies in $B$;
--
--   (i) $B$ is stable under $\mathrm{levelAutBar}\,q\,M'\,\zeta\,\gamma$ for every $\zeta \in \mathrm{Idx}\,q$ and every $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$;
--
--   (j) reduction to a Drinfeld curve: for every $\mathbb F_{q^2}$-algebra structure on $\kappa$, every proof that the coordinate ring $\mathrm{CoordRing}\,q\,\kappa = \kappa[x_0,x_1]/(\mathrm{drinfeldPoly} - 1)$ is a domain, and every $\zeta \in \mathrm{Idx}\,q$, there exist a subgroup $C_s$ of the group of $(q+1)$-st roots of unity of $\mathbb F_{q^2}$ and a ring homomorphism $\rho$ from $B$ to $\mathrm{quotField}\,q\,\kappa\,C_s$ — the fixed field, inside the Drinfeld function field $\mathrm{Frac}(\mathrm{CoordRing}\,q\,\kappa)$, of the subgroup generated by the actions of the elements $(1,\zeta')$ for $\zeta' \in C_s$ — such that: the cardinality of $C_s$ is $2\,\mathrm{placeWidthChar}\,q\,M'\,s$, where $\mathrm{placeWidthChar}$ is $\mathrm{jWidthChar}\,q$ of $s.\mathrm{evalAt}(j_{\mathrm{geom}})$ (for $q = 3$: $6$ at $j = 0$ and $1$ otherwise) divided by $\mathrm{placeRamificationJ}\,M'\,s$; the kernel of $\rho$ is the ideal generated by the image of $\varpi_b$; $\rho$ composed with the structure map $A_b \to B$ is the residue map $A \to \kappa$ followed by $\kappa \to \mathrm{quotField}\,q\,\kappa\,C_s$; every element of $\mathrm{quotField}\,q\,\kappa\,C_s$ is a quotient $\rho(g)/\rho(h)$ with $g, h \in B$ and $\rho(h) \ne 0$; an element $z$ of $\mathrm{quotField}\,q\,\kappa\,C_s$ lies in the range of $\rho$ if and only if $z$, viewed in the Drinfeld function field, lies in the image of $\mathrm{CoordRing}\,q\,\kappa$; and $\rho$ is equivariant in the sense that for $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$ with $(\mathrm{redQ}\,q\,\gamma, 1)$ in $\mathrm{hSubgroup}\,q$ (the kernel of the character sending $(g,u)$ to $\det(g)\,u^{q+1}$) and for $f \in B$ with $\mathrm{levelAutBar}\,q\,M'\,\zeta\,\gamma^{-1}(f) \in B$, the image $\rho(\mathrm{levelAutBar}\,q\,M'\,\zeta\,\gamma^{-1}(f))$ equals $\mathrm{hFunctionFieldAction}\,q\,\kappa$ at $(\mathrm{redQ}\,q\,\gamma,1)$ applied to $\rho(f)$, both read in the Drinfeld function field.
--
--   This is the construction of the affine chart (the local model) of the supersingular component of the semistable model of the full-level modular curve of level $q^2M'$ with $H$ the units congruent to $1$ modulo $q$, descended to the level field $F_0$ of functions with $q$-expansion coefficients in the small field $k_0$, in the case $q = 3$ and under the rigidity guard provided by an auxiliary prime $\ell_g \equiv 11 \pmod{12}$ dividing $M'$; the special fibre of the chart is identified with the affine coordinate ring of a quotient of a Drinfeld curve over $\kappa$, equivariantly for the level automorphisms. It is obtained from the variant [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.exists_supersingularDVR_affineChart_nodes_of_levelField_of_eq_three_of_dvd`](thm.html#ModularCurve.FullLevel.exists_supersingularDVR_affineChart_nodes_of_levelField_of_eq_three_of_dvd), which carries the same hypotheses, and it feeds [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.exists_klevel_supersingularDVR_affineChart_of_eq_three_of_dvd`](thm.html#ModularCurve.FullLevel.exists_klevel_supersingularDVR_affineChart_of_eq_three_of_dvd).
